WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.657
WITH CHECK OPTION enforces the view's filter for writes through the view.

00:00:05.657 --> 00:00:09.062
If an update would make a row no longer satisfy the active equals true condition,

00:00:09.062 --> 00:00:15.312
PostgreSQL rejects the write. This turns the filtered view into a more controlled write interface.

00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:20.982
It does not replace general database constraints or permissions.

00:00:20.982 --> 00:00:27.202
Some simple views can be updated because PostgreSQL can map each view row back to one base-table row.

00:00:27.202 --> 00:00:34.962
Filtered views introduce a policy question: should an update be allowed to move a row outside the view?

00:00:34.962 --> 00:00:38.720
WITH CHECK OPTION prevents writes that violate the view's own filter.
